    {
      "topic": "staff",
      "sentiment": "mixed",
      "mentions": 15,
      "title": {
        "en": "Helpful store associates alongside grooming friction"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Most shoppers describe retail associates and cashier staff as friendly and proactive, frequently singling out managers for hands-on assistance finding specific pet foods. However, several reviews highlight friction in the grooming salon, including disputes over surprise add-on charges, rigid policies regarding reactive dogs, and unannounced early closures of the wash station."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "place",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "mentions": 11,
      "title": {
        "en": "Comprehensive inventory and convenient amenities"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Customers appreciate the store's wide selection of dog and cat food, chew toys, and seasonal clearance items, noting the convenience of being located next to a grocery store. Reviewers also frequently use the self-service dog wash station. While one shopper criticized the tight shared parking lot, the retail floor is widely regarded as clean and well-stocked."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "animals",
      "sentiment": "mixed",
      "mentions": 5,
      "title": {
        "en": "Gentle grooming care with reactivity limits"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Multiple pet parents express deep gratitude for groomer Vanessa, noting that she handles anxious dogs with patience, gentle care, and attention to detail. Owners report that their pets return home calm, soft, and neatly trimmed. Conversely, one client voiced concern over stern handling and noted that the salon declined their reactive dog due to liability rules."
      }
    }
  ],
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": {
        "en": "Does Pet Supplies Plus on Lincoln Ave have a self-wash dog station?"
      },
      "a": {
        "en": "Yes, the store features a self-service dog wash station, though customers recommend arriving well before closing."
      },
